## Why This Is Asked
Tests data residency, tenant isolation, and end-to-end security in real-time inference.

## Key Concepts
- PrivateLink isolation and per-tenant KMS envelopes
- Tenant-scoped Feature Store and de-identification
- Canary rollouts and drift monitoring
- Rollback criteria and latency targets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo preprocessor: drop PII, hash identifiers
function preprocess(input, tenantId){
  const deid = deidentify(input);
  const keys = kms.getTenantKey(tenantId);
  return envelopeEncrypt(deid, keys);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test per-tenant key rotation without service interruption?
- What metrics would you use to trigger automatic rollbacks?
- How would you handle cross-tenant model version drift detection?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates knowledge of edge ML deployment, covering model optimization, over-the-air updates, and monitoring strategies for resource-constrained environments.

## Key Concepts
- Edge inference using SageMaker Edge Manager
- Model quantization (INT8) for ARM64 architecture
- OTA updates via AWS IoT Jobs with rollback slots
- Local telemetry and validation with intermittent connectivity

## Code Example
```javascript
// Model inference with latency tracking
const model = loadModel('arm_int8.tflite');
const t0 = performance.now();
const output = model.run(input);
const latency = performance.now() - t0;

// Emit telemetry for edge agent
emitTelemetry({ latency, outputQuality: evaluateQuality(output) });
```
